{"base_rate":0.29172141918528255,"brier":0.13099789750328517,"bss":0.3659961440104297,"bss_hi":0.49219413704597953,"bss_lo":0.22313239786064368,"chart":{"base":[314.2,145.0],"fp":[190.4,156.4],"lead":"62,256.1 272,228.1 482,194.9 692,151.3","note":{"base":"skill 0.37 — higher than 70% of cities","fp":"low end -2pp, high end +24pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.1 °C — better than 56% of cities","rel":"promised 2% → rained 1%; promised 91% → rained 67%"},"rel":"76.1,461.7 313.2,432.6 634.3,175.7"},"country":"JP","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.16593955321944812,"ess":421.30391799781603,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Nagoya</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Nagoya rain forecast is genuinely useful, though 4 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (97%), believe about\n<b>81%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>0%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 761 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nthe station, 5.6 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.37, ranked 64 of\n216 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(24&ndash;139) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>0%</b></td><td class='num'>229</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>9%</td><td class='num'><b>4%</b></td><td class='num'>69</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>29%</td><td class='num'><b>4%</b></td><td class='num'>79</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>51%</td><td class='num'><b>12%</b></td><td class='num'>76</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>71%</td><td class='num'><b>24%</b></td><td class='num'>76</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>97%</td><td class='num'><b>81%</b></td><td class='num'>232</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">4 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Nagoya</b> <span class=\"muted\">Japan</span></p>\n  <div class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag good\">Genuinely useful</span><details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What does this label mean?\" title=\"What does this label mean?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>Compared with a simple guess: saying &ldquo;29% chance of rain&rdquo; every day, because it rains here on 29% of days.</p><p>The forecast did clearly better.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details>\n    <span class=\"muted\">4 points off by more than chance</span></div>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score<details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What is the skill score?\" title=\"What is the skill score?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>How much better the forecast is than that simple guess. 0 means no better, 1 means perfect, below 0 means worse. Day-ahead rain forecasts usually score 0.3 to 0.5.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details></dt><dd>0.37</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>24&ndash;139\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 216</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>761 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Nagoya &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Nagoya\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"59.15938864628821,377.2314410480349 88.47478260869565,323.9710144927536 159.89822784810124,239.16455696202533 239.93736842105267,156.89473684210526 309.15368421052636,85.0526315789474 402.6464655172414,21.137931034482733 402.6464655172414,35.258620689655174 309.15368421052636,161.68421052631578 239.93736842105267,233.5263157894737 159.89822784810124,312.88607594936707 88.47478260869565,371.4492753623188 59.15938864628821,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"275.81340341655715\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"275.81340341655715\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"59.15938864628821,382.0 88.47478260869565,366.17391304347825 159.89822784810124,368.17721518987344 239.93736842105267,338.89473684210526 309.15368421052636,295.7894736842105 402.6464655172414,85.4655172413793\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 0% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 229 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"59.15938864628821\" cy=\"382.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 9%&amp;#10;It rained 4% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 69 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"88.47478260869565\" cy=\"366.17391304347825\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 29%&amp;#10;It rained 4% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 79 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"159.89822784810124\" cy=\"368.17721518987344\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 51%&amp;#10;It rained 12% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 76 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"239.93736842105267\" cy=\"338.89473684210526\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 71%&amp;#10;It rained 24% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 76 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"309.15368421052636\" cy=\"295.7894736842105\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 97%&amp;#10;It rained 81% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 232 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"402.6464655172414\" cy=\"85.4655172413793\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(29%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Nagoya the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>spring</b> (0.64) and least in\n<b>winter</b> (-0.39).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>175</td><td class='num'>12%</td><td class='num'>-0.394</td><td class='num'>22.4%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>182</td><td class='num'>33%</td><td class='num'>0.274</td><td class='num'>15.0%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>31%</td><td class='num'>0.332</td><td class='num'>21.7%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>220</td><td class='num'>38%</td><td class='num'>0.644</td><td class='num'>8.9%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":35.18147,"lon":136.90641,"n":761,"n_cities":216,"name":"Nagoya","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.030000000000000283,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0032751091703056767,"n":229,"obs":0.0,"sig":false},{"hi":0.16,"lo":0.030000000000000283,"mean":0.08608695652173913,"n":69,"obs":0.043478260869565216,"sig":false},{"hi":0.43,"lo":0.16,"mean":0.2878481012658227,"n":79,"obs":0.0379746835443038,"sig":true},{"hi":0.61,"lo":0.43,"mean":0.5139473684210527,"n":76,"obs":0.11842105263157894,"sig":true},{"hi":0.82,"lo":0.61,"mean":0.7094736842105265,"n":76,"obs":0.23684210526315788,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.82,"mean":0.9735775862068966,"n":232,"obs":0.8146551724137931,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":5.6,"provisional":false,"rank":64,"rank_hi":139.0,"rank_lo":24.0,"reliability":0.05228139806555939,"resolution":0.12454793525458191,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"nagoya","station":"","timezone":"Asia/Tokyo"}